<title>MALAYSIA: MALAYSIA STOCKS - factors to watch - Feb 26.</title>
<headline>MALAYSIA STOCKS - factors to watch - Feb 26.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are some of the main factors likely to affect Malaysian stocks on Wednesday:</p>
<p>* On Tuesday, the Dow Jones rose 30.01 points to 7,038.21.</p>
<p>* The Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange Composite Index of 100 large-capitalisation stocks gained 6.10 points to 1,271.00.</p>
<p>* Nikkei Stock Average was up 130.37 points to 19,200.44 at 0021 GMT.</p>
<p>* Malaysian Resources holds annual general meeting.  </p>
<p>In overnight news:</p>
<p>* Malaysia's 1996 trade deficit shrank to 617.97 million ringgit from a gap of 9.36 billion ringgit in 1995.</p>
<p>* Genting and unit, Resorts World both posted a 4.0 percent rise in 1996 net profit.</p>
<p>* Asiatic Development reported an 11 percent decline in 1996 net profit.</p>
<p>* OSK Holdings posted a sharp increase in 1996 net profit, and proposed a one-for-one bonus issue and a special issue of 26.9 million shares at 5.0 ringgit each to Bumiputra (ethnic Malay) shareholders.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
